## Core C++ Types

| Type | Role for MCP |
| --- | --- |
| `UAnimBlueprint` | AnimBP asset. Use `GetAnimBlueprintGeneratedClass()` instead of Python `generated_class` guesses. |
| `UAnimBlueprintFactory` | Editor factory for sample AnimBP creation with `TargetSkeleton`, `PreviewSkeletalMesh`, and `ParentClass`. |
| `UAnimBlueprintGeneratedClass` | Compiled AnimBP class and runtime-node mapping boundary. |
| `USkeleton` / `USkeletalMesh` | Source assets for sample AnimBP creation and PhysicsAsset lookup. |
| `UAnimGraphNode_Base` | Editor visual node base for pose-generating/pose-consuming AnimGraph nodes. |
| `FAnimNode_Base` | Runtime node struct paired with editor AnimGraph nodes. |
| `UEdGraph` / `UEdGraphNode` / `UEdGraphPin` | Graph topology, node placement, pin direction, default values, and links. |
| `UAnimGraphNode_ControlRig` | Editor ControlRig AnimGraph node wrapping `FAnimNode_ControlRig`. |
| `FAnimNode_ControlRig` | Runtime ControlRig node struct in AnimGraph evaluation. Use `SetControlRigClass()` in C++ rather than Python property guesses. |
| `UControlRigBlueprint` | ControlRig asset/editor surface. |
| `UControlRigBlueprintFactory` | Editor factory for sample ControlRig Blueprint creation. |
| `UControlRigBlueprintEditorLibrary` | Editor helper surface for preview mesh, hierarchy, hierarchy controller, and initialization. |
| `UControlRig` | Runtime/transient rig instance. Useful for direct gate probes. |
| `URigVMController` | RigVM graph mutation authority. |
| `URigVMGraph` / `URigVMNode` / `URigVMUnitNode` / `URigVMPin` / `URigVMLink` | RigVM graph, node, unit-node, pin, and link readback surfaces used by `inspect_controlrig_rigvm_topology`; `URigVMGraph::CanLink` and pin/link lookup APIs are used by `validate_controlrig_rigvm_links` without authoring links; `URigVMPin::CanProvideDefaultValue`, `IsValidDefaultValue`, and `ClampDefaultValueFromMetaData` are used by `validate_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` without setting values. |
| `URigVMController` | RigVM mutation authority. Current MCP writer scope is limited to sample/temp `AddLink()` through `add_controlrig_rigvm_links` and sample/temp `SetPinDefaultValue()` through `set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults`; arbitrary nodes, variables, functions, comments, reroutes, exposed pins, graph replacement, cast-node creation, and original asset mutation remain out of scope. |
| `FRigUnit_BeginExecution`, `FRigUnit_PreBeginExecution`, `FRigUnit_PostBeginExecution`, `FRigUnit_PrepareForExecution`, `FRigUnit_PostPrepareForExecution`, `FRigUnit_InverseExecution` | UE 5.6.1 public single-instance ControlRig event units allowlisted for `ensure_controlrig_sample_asset.unit_nodes`. Local UE 5.6.1 headers do not expose `FRigUnit_EndExecution`; do not synthesize it. `FRigUnit_InteractionExecution` is public but not allowlisted because it does not declare `CanOnlyExistOnce()`. `FRigUnit_SequenceExecution` is deprecated and not allowlisted. |
| `URigHierarchy` | Hierarchy read surface for bones, controls, nulls, and curves. |
| `URigHierarchyController` | Hierarchy mutation authority. |
| `UAnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimGraph` | Editor linked AnimBP instance node wrapping `FAnimNode_LinkedAnimGraph`. |
| `UAnimGraphNode_LinkedAnimLayer` | Editor linked layer node wrapping `FAnimNode_LinkedAnimLayer`. |
| `UAnimGraphNode_LinkedInputPose` | Editor linked input pose node; compiler/schema must reconcile pins and function references. |
| `FAnimNode_LinkedAnimGraph` | Runtime linked AnimGraph node with `InstanceClass` and generated input pose links. |
| `FAnimNode_LinkedAnimLayer` | Runtime linked layer node with `Interface` and `Layer` fields. |
| `UAnimLayerInterface` | Interface type for linked Anim Layer signatures. |
| `UPhysicsAsset` | Static PhysicsAsset source for bodies, constraints, profiles, and RBAN solver settings. |
| `USkeletalBodySetup` | Per-body collision setup and physical animation profile surface. |
| `UPhysicsConstraintTemplate` | Per-constraint source containing `DefaultInstance` and profile handles. |
| `FConstraintInstance` | Constraint bone names, linear/angular limits, projection, breakability, plasticity, and drives. |

## Python API Surfaces That Are Useful

Use Unreal Python where it is an exposed, documented editor API:

- load `ControlRigDeveloper` before ControlRig editing;
- load existing `ControlRigBlueprint` assets;
- use `ControlRigBlueprint.get_currently_open_rig_blueprints()`;
- use `ControlRigBlueprintFactory` for new sample ControlRig assets;
- set preview meshes on ControlRig assets;
- use ControlRig Python Log output as a source for rig graph/hierarchy commands;
- query documented `ControlRigBlueprint`, `RigHierarchy`, and `RigVMController`
  methods when building safe sample-only scripts.

Do not assume the same Python access model works for protected AnimGraph
internals.

## Current MCP Command Surface

Use these before considering new C++:

| Need | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Static AnimGraph topology | `inspect_anim_graph_protected_topology` |
| Reflected runtime `FAnimNode_*` settings | `inspect_anim_graph_node_settings` |
| State-machine transitions and rule graphs | `inspect_anim_state_machine_transitions` |
| Source animation notifies, curves, sync markers, and Montage layout | `inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded` |
| ControlRig gate behavior on a transient rig | `controlrig_direct_gate_probe` |
| Direct transient ControlRig pre/post transforms | `sample_controlrig_pre_post_runtime_pose` |
| Read-only skeleton profile and recipe-planning evidence | `profile_controlrig_skeleton` |
| Deterministic skeleton-profile to controls-only recipe planning | `compile_controlrig_profile_recipe` |
| ControlRig recipe transaction report and failure/reuse evidence | `validate_controlrig_recipe`, `dry_run_controlrig_recipe`, `build_controlrig_recipe` |
| ControlRig RigVM topology, link feasibility, and pin-default feasibility | `inspect_controlrig_rigvm_topology`, then `validate_controlrig_rigvm_links` or `validate_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` |
| Sample/temp ControlRig RigVM link or pin-default authoring | Validate first, then `add_controlrig_rigvm_links` or `set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` on `/Game/_MCP_Sample` or `/Game/_MCP_Temp` only |
| Live AnimGraph target resolver and PoseWatch proof | `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose` with `mapping_support` diagnostics for attribution support class and evidence tier |
| Live SkeletalMeshComponent bones/sockets | `sample_skeletal_bones_in_sie` |
| BlendSpace runtime pose grid | `sample_blendspace_runtime_pose_grid` |
| Sample/temp BlendSpace variant authoring | `ensure_blendspace_sample_variant`; planner/job-contract route `blendspace_sample_variant` targets `_MCP_Temp` and verifies with `sample_blendspace_runtime_pose_grid` |
| Sample-only AnimBP creation from Skeleton/SkeletalMesh | `create_anim_blueprint_sample` |
| Sample-only AnimBP state-machine authoring | `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant` |
| Sample-only AnimBP locomotion EventGraph variable driving | `ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver` |
| Planner-composed sample locomotion AnimBP | `anim_bp_locomotion_sample_pipeline` in `bp_authoring_job_contract.py`, chaining the EventGraph driver and state-machine authoring commands |
| Sample-only ControlRig AnimGraph node insertion | `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample` |
| Sample-only Linked Anim Graph composition | `ensure_linked_anim_graph_sample_variant` |
| Live AnimInstance state read | `inspect_anim_instance_runtime_state` |
| Runtime-only AnimInstance property probe | `set_anim_instance_runtime_property_for_probe` |
| State-machine runtime response probe | `sample_anim_state_machine_runtime_response` |
| Sample Post Process input-pose passthrough | `ensure_anim_graph_input_pose_passthrough` |
| Sample Post Process ModifyBone chain | `ensure_anim_graph_modify_bone_demo` |
| Sample ModifyCurve chain | `ensure_anim_graph_modify_curve_demo` |
| ControlRig input default exposure in sample AnimBP | `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` |
| Forced driver sample around ControlRig node | `ensure_controlrig_forced_driver_animbp` |
| Sample Trail Controller chain | `ensure_anim_graph_trail_demo` |
| Sample RigidBody settings | `set_anim_graph_rigidbody_settings` |
| PhysicsAsset bodies, constraints, profiles, and RBAN solver settings | `inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded` |
| SkeletalMeshComponent AnimBP defaults | `set_skeletal_mesh_component_anim_defaults` |

## New C++ Bridge Triggers

Add or modify UnrealMCP C++ only when a concrete request hits one of these:

- protected AnimGraph topology must be read or written and no command covers it;
- ControlRig optional pins or custom property bindings must be exposed safely;
- compiled editor-node to runtime-node mapping fails for a required node class;
- same-instance pre/post proof is required for a node class that still cannot be
  attributed after checking `sample_anim_node_pre_post_runtime_pose.mapping_support`;
  first check
  `Docs/Research/extend_anim_node_runtime_mapping_design.md`;
- a sample AnimBP needs arbitrary ControlRig node insertion beyond
  `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`, such as inserting before/after a
  selected node or broad graph rewrites;
- advanced state-machine authoring is required beyond
  `ensure_anim_state_machine_sample_variant` support, such as conduits, state
  aliases, nested machines, custom transition graphs, arbitrary rule graphs
  beyond bounded bool/float/enum variable rules and bounded BlendSpacePlayer
  input bindings, or
  replacing/deleting an existing machine;
- EventGraph variable driving is required beyond the bounded
  `ensure_anim_bp_event_graph_locomotion_driver`
  Speed/Direction/IsInAir/Acceleration/IsAccelerating route, such as gait,
  turn-in-place, or arbitrary EventGraph rewrites;
- sequence notify, curve, sync marker, or Montage internals are required; use
  `inspect_animation_asset_metadata_guarded` first;
- PhysicsAsset body, constraint, limit, drive, or profile data is required; use
  `inspect_physics_asset_constraints_guarded` first;
- a sample ControlRig asset must be created or seeded with preview/hierarchy
  data; first check
  `Docs/Research/ensure_controlrig_sample_asset_design.md`;
- linked Anim Graph, linked Anim Layer, or Sub Anim Instance sample authoring is
  required; first check
  `Docs/Research/linked_anim_graph_layer_sample_authoring_design.md`;
- repeated manual setup becomes riskier than a narrow guarded command.

Every new bridge command should be editor-only, guarded, structured, and
sample-root-first.

